# Prospective actual relative-density domain, not a sealed statement

This is root-authored mathematical target design only. No SAU claim, statement
seal, implementation or proof search has occurred. Exclusive compiler lease
currently belongs to the current31 independent repository verifier.

Generic authored background is finite-dimensional real Hilbert Gaussian-Gibbs
calculus with C2 convex rho, stationary normalized origin, finite nonnegative
Hessian upper bound. It includes L=0 and dimension0. The genuine SPHMC consumer
produces rho and the same actual standardized true RGO from the source V and
every positive eta. It receives no normalizer, law, Fisher, density, integrability,
LSI, T2, selector or mean certificate.

The new mathematical delta is actual positive relative density and square-root
representative, entropy integrability, true relative log-gradient, and the
one-quarter Fisher-to-Dirichlet identity, with all L2 domains internal.
This is classical C2/L2 representative-domain work. It does not establish an
arbitrary Radon-Nikodym representative's pointwise differentiability, a weak
Sobolev framework, Gaussian LSI, Talagrand T2, full first(4.6), bias(4.2), either
main theorem, work, or composition.

Future proposal must bind the repaired preread graph/inventory/contract and the
distinct repaired topology review, not the original historical dependency-ready
packet. Exact signatures require type-only focused validation and independent
statement/binder/definition review before proof search. A genuine source theorem
using these domains will need real Gaussian LSI/T2 producers and explicit
carrier, energy, entropy/KL and metric adapters; these remain open.
